        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(goals): preserve durable owner across completion wakes",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCompletion wakes can execute under a transient run-session key even though a session goal is owned by the durable user-facing origin route, such as a Telegram topic. Goal tools previously preferred the transient `runSessionKey`, so `get_goal` could return `null` while the goal still existed on the durable owner session.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nGoal tool scope resolution now prefers a concrete `agentSessionKey`, which represents the durable owning thread, and uses the run-session key only for legacy `global` contexts or when no owner key exists. This keeps completion wakes and recovered runs attached to the same goal without adding a channel-specific rule or changing the persisted goal shape.\n\nThe change is intentionally limited to core goal owner resolution, its focused regression coverage, and the directly coupled goal documentation.\n\n## User Impact\n\n`get_goal`, `create_goal`, and `update_goal` continue to resolve the durable thread goal when execution temporarily runs under another session key. Existing structured goals require no migration.\n\nCompatibility limitation: legacy goals containing only an objective plus an external Markdown checklist do not contain a structured executable phase ledger. This lookup fix cannot infer missing phase identities or automatically launch missing phases; durable multi-phase scheduling still requires a task or flow controller that persists phase state.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/goal-tools.test.ts` — 1 file passed, 4 tests passed.\n- `pnpm docs:list` — completed.\n- `pnpm docs:check-mdx` — passed (705 files).\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` — passed.\n- Repository autoreview against `origin/main` — clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Remote `check:changed` could not start: Blacksmith is not authenticated in this environment, and the configured AWS Crabbox broker is unavailable. PR CI remains the broader validation path.\n\n",
